# Commit as the personal account, never the work one

This is a personal project. Every commit must be authored by **johnbekele**:

```
user.name  = John Bekele
user.email = 164889902+johnbekele@users.noreply.github.com
```

These are set in the repository's local git config, which every worktree shares. Do not remove them
and do not let a commit fall through to the global config: that carries
`yohans.bekele@thomsonreuters.com`, which GitHub resolves to the work account `johnbekele6130593`,
and attributes personal work to an employer.

Check before your first commit in a session:

```bash
git config --get user.email   # must be 164889902+johnbekele@users.noreply.github.com
```

If commits were already made with the wrong address and are not yet merged, rewrite them before the
pull request is reviewed:

```bash
git rebase --exec 'git commit --amend --no-edit --reset-author' origin/main
git log origin/main..HEAD --format='%an <%ae>'   # verify
```

`gh` is authenticated as `johnbekele` and is the only permitted profile for issues, pull requests
and any other remote operation. Never add an AI or assistant co-author trailer; Gate 2 rejects them.
